[start-outcomes] After this part you should be able to
1. name the types of retaining wall and the three ways a wall fails the ground, and give a cantilever wall its first dimensions;
2. find the active pressure of Rankine with a surcharge, the two thrusts and their lines of action, and tabulate every load on the wall with its moment about the toe;
3. check overturning (EQU) and sliding, in combination 1 and in EC7 Combination 2, with the right partial factor on every load;
4. find where the resultant meets the base, check the middle third and the bearing pressure, and change the toe or the heel so that the wall passes every check.
